-- Independent tests of the 2023 Merger Guidelines encoding (U.S. DOJ and FTC, 18 December 2023).
-- AGENCY ENFORCEMENT POLICY, NOT LAW.
--
-- Written by an independent test author who read the source text first and wrote the expected answers down
-- (scratch answers.md) before opening this encoding. Only the exported names and signatures were then taken from
-- the encoding; none of its tests or fixtures were read or imported. Each group cites the provision and the
-- `[pdf page N of 51]` of registers/source-bundle/2023-merger-guidelines.txt that the answer comes from.
--
-- A FAILING assertion here is a finding, left failing on purpose. Do not "fix" it by editing this file to match the
-- encoding; read the cited provision and decide whether the encoding or this reading is wrong.
--
-- Answer ids in brackets ([D7], [K10]) refer to the author's answers.md. Where the text is silent the assertion is
-- the weakest claim the text supports: "is NOTHING", or "is not JUST TRUE", never a bare FALSE.
-- Target dialect: main. Helper names start with `ind ` so they cannot collide with the encoding's names.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `mg-nouns`
IMPORT `mg-concentration`
IMPORT `mg-frameworks`
IMPORT `mg-rebuttal`
IMPORT `mg-tools`

§ `Independent tests`

§§ `helpers`

GIVEN m IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      lo IS A NUMBER
      hi IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- TRUE only for JUST x with lo <= x <= hi; NOTHING is FALSE, so this is used only where a number is expected.
`ind within` MEANS
    CONSIDER m
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST x THEN x AT LEAST lo AND x AT MOST hi

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      s IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF `Firm in the relevant market`
`ind fringe of` MEANS
    IF n AT MOST 0
    THEN EMPTY
    ELSE `a rival with a share of` "fringe" s FOLLOWED BY `ind fringe of` (n MINUS 1) s

GIVETH A `Guideline 1 presumption`
`ind PRESUME` MEANS `the Agencies presume the merger may substantially lessen competition, unless sufficiently disproved or rebutted`

GIVETH A `Guideline 1 presumption`
`ind NO PRESUMPTION` MEANS `no structural presumption arises under Guideline 1, and the other Guidelines may still apply`

-- Field readers for a MAYBE `Guideline 1 finding`: NOTHING stays NOTHING.
GIVEN m IS A MAYBE `Guideline 1 finding`
GIVETH A MAYBE `Guideline 1 presumption`
`ind presumption in` MEANS
    CONSIDER m
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST f THEN JUST (f's `the presumption`)

GIVEN m IS A MAYBE `Guideline 1 finding`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`ind pre HHI in` MEANS
    CONSIDER m
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST f THEN JUST (f's `pre-merger HHI`)

GIVEN m IS A MAYBE `Guideline 1 finding`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`ind post HHI in` MEANS
    CONSIDER m
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST f THEN JUST (f's `post-merger HHI`)

GIVEN m IS A MAYBE `Guideline 1 finding`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`ind change in` MEANS
    CONSIDER m
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST f THEN JUST (f's `change in HHI`)

GIVEN m IS A MAYBE `Guideline 1 finding`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`ind merged share in` MEANS
    CONSIDER m
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST f THEN JUST (f's `merged firm's share`)

GIVEN m IS A MAYBE `Guideline 1 finding`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ind HHI limb in` MEANS
    CONSIDER m
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST f THEN JUST (f's `the HHI limb is met`)

GIVEN m IS A MAYBE `Guideline 1 finding`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ind share limb in` MEANS
    CONSIDER m
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST f THEN JUST (f's `the share limb is met`)

GIVEN m IS A MAYBE `Guideline 1 finding`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ind highly concentrated in` MEANS
    CONSIDER m
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST f THEN JUST (f's `highly concentrated after the merger`)

GIVEN m IS A MAYBE `Guideline 1 finding`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ind significant increase in` MEANS
    CONSIDER m
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST f THEN JUST (f's `significant increase in concentration`)

GIVEN market IS A LIST OF `Firm in the relevant market`
GIVETH A MAYBE `Guideline 1 finding`
`ind G1` MEANS `the Agencies' reading under Guideline 1 of` market

-- Signature patch, 2026-11-25, by the encoding's builder at the parent session's ruling (NOTES.md section 10): the band,
-- the two limbs and the presumption on the metrics now return a MAYBE. These unwrap it for the assertions below. Each has
-- no NOTHING branch on purpose: a NOTHING raises eval/non-exhaustive-patterns, so it fails loudly and can never satisfy
-- an assertion, NOT (...) included.
GIVEN h IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Concentration band`
`ind band of` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the concentration band of an HHI of` h
    WHEN JUST b THEN b

GIVEN post IS A NUMBER
      change IS A NUMBER
      share IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Guideline 1 presumption`
`ind presumption on the metrics` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the Guideline 1 presumption on the metrics` post change share
    WHEN JUST p THEN p

GIVEN post IS A NUMBER
      change IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`ind HHI limb` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the HHI limb of the presumption is met by` post change
    WHEN JUST b THEN b

GIVEN share IS A NUMBER
      change IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`ind share limb` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the share limb of the presumption is met by` share change
    WHEN JUST b THEN b

§§ `A. HHI arithmetic: section 2.1 [pdf page 6 of 51], footnote 13 [pdf page 6], footnote 14 [pdf page 7]`

-- [A2] "reaching 10,000 in a market with a single firm".
#ASSERT `the HHI of the shares` (LIST 100) EQUALS 10000
-- [A3] footnote 13: five equal firms, 5 x 20^2 = 2,000.
#ASSERT `the HHI of the shares` (LIST 20, 20, 20, 20, 20) EQUALS 2000
-- [A4] footnote 13: six equal firms about 1,667, exact shares 100/6.
#ASSERT `ind within` (JUST (`the HHI of the shares` (LIST 100 DIVIDED BY 6, 100 DIVIDED BY 6, 100 DIVIDED BY 6, 100 DIVIDED BY 6, 100 DIVIDED BY 6, 100 DIVIDED BY 6))) 1666.5 1667.5
-- [A4] footnote 13 as printed: 6 x 16.67^2 = 1,667.
#ASSERT `ind within` (JUST (`the HHI of the shares` (LIST 16.67, 16.67, 16.67, 16.67, 16.67, 16.67))) 1666.5 1667.5
-- [A5] ten equal firms: 10 x 10^2 = 1,000.
#ASSERT `the HHI of the shares` (LIST 10, 10, 10, 10, 10, 10, 10, 10, 10, 10) EQUALS 1000
-- [A7] footnote 14 worked example: 20% and 5% give 2 x 20 x 5 = 200.
#ASSERT `the change in HHI from merging firms with shares` 20 5 EQUALS 200
#ASSERT `the change in HHI from merging firms with shares` 5 20 EQUALS 200
-- [A8]
#ASSERT `the change in HHI from merging firms with shares` 20 20 EQUALS 800

§§ `B. Concentration bands: section 2.1 [pdf page 6 of 51], footnote 15 [pdf page 7], footnote 21 [pdf page 11]`

-- [B1-B3] "greater than 1,800": 1,800 itself is NOT highly concentrated.
#ASSERT `highly concentrated, by an HHI of` 2000
#ASSERT NOT (`highly concentrated, by an HHI of` 1800)
#ASSERT `highly concentrated, by an HHI of` 1801
#ASSERT `highly concentrated, by an HHI of` 1800.01
-- [B5, B6] footnote 21 "HHI greater than 1,000": 1,000 itself is NOT concentrated.
#ASSERT NOT (`concentrated, by an HHI of` 1000)
#ASSERT `concentrated, by an HHI of` 1001
#ASSERT `concentrated, by an HHI of` 1800
-- [B2, B4, B5, B7] the bands.
#ASSERT `ind band of` 2000 EQUALS `highly concentrated (HHI greater than 1,800)`
#ASSERT `ind band of` 1800 EQUALS `concentrated but not highly concentrated (HHI greater than 1,000, at most 1,800)`
#ASSERT `ind band of` 1667 EQUALS `concentrated but not highly concentrated (HHI greater than 1,000, at most 1,800)`
#ASSERT `ind band of` 1000 EQUALS `not concentrated (HHI at most 1,000)`
#ASSERT `ind band of` 909 EQUALS `not concentrated (HHI at most 1,000)`

§§ `C. Significant increase and the thirty percent share: section 2.1 [pdf pages 6 and 7 of 51]`

-- [C1-C3] "a change of more than 100 points": exactly 100 is NOT significant.
#ASSERT `a significant increase, by a change in HHI of` 101
#ASSERT NOT (`a significant increase, by a change in HHI of` 100)
#ASSERT `a significant increase, by a change in HHI of` 100.5
#ASSERT `a significant increase, by a change in HHI of` 200
-- "a share over thirty percent": exactly 30 is NOT over.
#ASSERT NOT (`a merged firm's share over thirty percent, by a share of` 30)
#ASSERT `a merged firm's share over thirty percent, by a share of` 30.01
#ASSERT `a merged firm's share over thirty percent, by a share of` 31

