§§ `K. Failing firm: 3.1 [pdf page 31 of 51]; footnote 62 [pdf pages 31 and 32]`

-- Parameters: price, less severe danger, keeps assets in the market, rejected.
GIVEN price IS A NUMBER
      less IS A BOOLEAN
      keep IS A BOOLEAN
      rejected IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Alternative offer`
`ind offer` MEANS `Alternative offer` WITH
    `the price offered for the assets` IS price
    `the offer poses a less severe danger to competition than the proposed merger` IS less
    `the offer would keep the assets in the relevant market` IS keep
    `the offer was rejected` IS rejected

-- Parameters: unable to meet obligations, evidence is declining sales or losses standing alone, unable to reorganize,
-- good-faith efforts before the claim, liquidation value, offers.
GIVEN unable IS A BOOLEAN
      alone IS A BOOLEAN
      noreorg IS A BOOLEAN
      efforts IS A BOOLEAN
      liq IS A NUMBER
      offers IS A LIST OF `Alternative offer`
GIVETH A `Failing firm claim`
`ind FF claim` MEANS `Failing firm claim` WITH
    `the evidence shows that the firm would be unable to meet its financial obligations in the near future` IS unable
    `the evidence of failure is declining sales or net losses standing alone` IS alone
    `the evidence suggests that the firm would be unable to reorganize successfully under Chapter 11` IS noreorg
    `the evidence shows good-faith efforts, before the claim, to elicit reasonable alternative offers` IS efforts
    `the liquidation value of the assets` IS liq
    `the alternative offers received` IS offers

GIVEN m IS A MAYBE `Failing firm finding`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ind FF accept in` MEANS
    CONSIDER m
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST f THEN JUST (f's `the Agencies accept the failing firm defense`)

GIVEN m IS A MAYBE `Failing firm finding`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ind FF rejected in` MEANS
    CONSIDER m
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST f THEN JUST (f's `a reasonable alternative offer was rejected, so the business cannot be claimed failing`)

-- [K6] footnote 62: "Any offer ... for a price above the liquidation value ... will be regarded as a reasonable
-- alternative offer."
#ASSERT `the offer is a reasonable alternative offer, by footnote 62` (`ind offer` 101 TRUE TRUE TRUE) 100 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the offer is above liquidation value` (`ind offer` 101 TRUE TRUE TRUE) 100
-- [K7, K8] at or below liquidation value: footnote 62 does not deem it reasonable; otherwise text silent.
#ASSERT NOT (`the offer is a reasonable alternative offer, by footnote 62` (`ind offer` 100 TRUE TRUE TRUE) 100 EQUALS JUST TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the offer is above liquidation value` (`ind offer` 100 TRUE TRUE TRUE) 100)
#ASSERT NOT (`the offer is a reasonable alternative offer, by footnote 62` (`ind offer` 50 TRUE TRUE TRUE) 100 EQUALS JUST TRUE)

-- [K4] all three requirements, no offer received despite good-faith efforts: the defence is available.
#ASSERT `requirement A of the failing firm defense is shown` (`ind FF claim` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE 100 EMPTY)
#ASSERT `requirement B of the failing firm defense is shown` (`ind FF claim` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE 100 EMPTY)
#ASSERT `requirement C of the failing firm defense is shown` (`ind FF claim` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE 100 EMPTY)
#ASSERT `ind FF accept in` (`the Agencies' reading of the failing firm claim` (`ind FF claim` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE 100 EMPTY)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- [K1, K5] requirement A missing.
#ASSERT NOT (`requirement A of the failing firm defense is shown` (`ind FF claim` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE 100 EMPTY))
#ASSERT `ind FF accept in` (`the Agencies' reading of the failing firm claim` (`ind FF claim` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE 100 EMPTY)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- [K1] "Declining sales and/or net losses, standing alone, are insufficient."
#ASSERT NOT (`requirement A of the failing firm defense is shown` (`ind FF claim` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE 100 EMPTY))
#ASSERT `ind FF accept in` (`the Agencies' reading of the failing firm claim` (`ind FF claim` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE 100 EMPTY)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- [K2, K5] requirement B missing.
#ASSERT NOT (`requirement B of the failing firm defense is shown` (`ind FF claim` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE 100 EMPTY))
#ASSERT `ind FF accept in` (`the Agencies' reading of the failing firm claim` (`ind FF claim` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE 100 EMPTY)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- [K11] "Parties must solicit reasonable alternative offers before claiming that the business is failing."
#ASSERT NOT (`requirement C of the failing firm defense is shown` (`ind FF claim` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE 100 EMPTY))
#ASSERT `ind FF accept in` (`the Agencies' reading of the failing firm claim` (`ind FF claim` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE 100 EMPTY)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- [K10] "If a reasonable alternative offer was rejected, the parties cannot claim that the business is failing."
#ASSERT `a reasonable alternative offer was rejected` (LIST `ind offer` 150 TRUE TRUE TRUE) 100
#ASSERT `ind FF rejected in` (`the Agencies' reading of the failing firm claim` (`ind FF claim` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE 100 (LIST `ind offer` 150 TRUE TRUE TRUE))) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `ind FF accept in` (`the Agencies' reading of the failing firm claim` (`ind FF claim` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE 100 (LIST `ind offer` 150 TRUE TRUE TRUE))) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- [K3] a reasonable, less dangerous offer still open: the acquirer is not "the only available purchaser".
#ASSERT `ind FF accept in` (`the Agencies' reading of the failing firm claim` (`ind FF claim` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE 100 (LIST `ind offer` 150 TRUE TRUE FALSE))) EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `L. Failing division: footnote 64 [pdf page 32 of 51]`

-- Parameters: negative cash flow, economically justified, evidence solely management plans, good-faith efforts,
-- liquidation value, offers.
GIVEN negative IS A BOOLEAN
      justified IS A BOOLEAN
      plans IS A BOOLEAN
      efforts IS A BOOLEAN
      liq IS A NUMBER
      offers IS A LIST OF `Alternative offer`
GIVETH A `Failing division claim`
`ind FD claim` MEANS `Failing division claim` WITH
    `on cost allocation reflecting true economic costs, the division has a persistently negative operating cash flow` IS negative
    `the negative cash flow is economically justified for the firm by benefits such as complementary sales or goodwill` IS justified
    `the evidence rests solely on management plans that could have been prepared for the purpose` IS plans
    `the owner made good-faith efforts to elicit reasonable alternative offers` IS efforts
    `the liquidation value of the division's assets` IS liq
    `the alternative offers for the division` IS offers

GIVEN m IS A MAYBE `Failing division finding`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ind FD credit in` MEANS
    CONSIDER m
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST f THEN JUST (f's `the Agencies may credit the claim that the division's assets would exit`)

-- [L1, L2] both conditions met.
#ASSERT `condition 1 of footnote 64 is shown` (`ind FD claim` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE 100 EMPTY)
#ASSERT `condition 2 of footnote 64 is shown` (`ind FD claim` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE 100 EMPTY)
#ASSERT `ind FD credit in` (`the Agencies' reading of the failing division claim` (`ind FD claim` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE 100 EMPTY)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- [L1] no persistently negative cash flow.
#ASSERT `ind FD credit in` (`the Agencies' reading of the failing division claim` (`ind FD claim` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 100 EMPTY)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- [L4] negative but economically justified by complementary sales or goodwill.
#ASSERT NOT (`condition 1 of footnote 64 is shown` (`ind FD claim` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE 100 EMPTY))
#ASSERT `ind FD credit in` (`the Agencies' reading of the failing division claim` (`ind FD claim` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE 100 EMPTY)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- [L3] evidence solely management plans that could have been prepared for the purpose.
#ASSERT `ind FD credit in` (`the Agencies' reading of the failing division claim` (`ind FD claim` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE 100 EMPTY)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- [L2] no good-faith efforts.
#ASSERT NOT (`condition 2 of footnote 64 is shown` (`ind FD claim` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 100 EMPTY))
#ASSERT `ind FD credit in` (`the Agencies' reading of the failing division claim` (`ind FD claim` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 100 EMPTY)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- [L2] the efforts were not "unsuccessful": they elicited a reasonable, less dangerous offer keeping the assets in the
-- market, which was rejected.
#ASSERT `ind FD credit in` (`the Agencies' reading of the failing division claim` (`ind FD claim` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE 100 (LIST `ind offer` 150 TRUE TRUE TRUE))) EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `M. Entry and repositioning: 3.2 [pdf pages 32 and 33 of 51]; footnote 65 [pdf page 32]`

GIVEN name IS A STRING
      scale IS A BOOLEAN
      strength IS A BOOLEAN
      durability IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Entrant compared with a merging party`
`ind compared` MEANS `Entrant compared with a merging party` WITH
    `the merging party compared` IS name
    `the entry replicates its scale` IS scale
    `the entry replicates its strength` IS strength
    `the entry replicates its durability` IS durability

-- Parameters: response, time to replace, time to effect, durable, likely, comparisons, depends on lessening
-- competition elsewhere, repositioning reduces competition in source markets.
GIVEN response IS A `Supply response`
      replace IS A NUMBER
      effect IS A NUMBER
      durable IS A BOOLEAN
      likely IS A BOOLEAN
      comparisons IS A LIST OF `Entrant compared with a merging party`
      elsewhere IS A BOOLEAN
      reduces IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Entry claim`
`ind entry claim` MEANS `Entry claim` WITH
    `the response claimed` IS response
    `time until the entry would replace the lost competition` IS replace
    `time until any effect from the loss of competition may occur` IS effect
    `the entry would be durable` IS durable
    `the entry is so likely that no substantial lessening of competition is threatened` IS likely
    `comparisons with the merging parties` IS comparisons
    `the entry depends on lessening competition in other markets` IS elsewhere
    `the repositioning would reduce competition in the markets the products are moved from` IS reduces

GIVETH A LIST OF `Entrant compared with a merging party`
`ind replicates A` MEANS LIST `ind compared` "A" TRUE TRUE TRUE

GIVEN m IS A MAYBE `Entry finding`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ind entry credit in` MEANS
    CONSIDER m
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST f THEN JUST (f's `the Agencies credit the entry or repositioning rebuttal`)

-- [M1] timely, likely and sufficient: credited.
#ASSERT `the entry is timely` (`ind entry claim` `entry` 6 12 TRUE TRUE `ind replicates A` FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the entry is likely` (`ind entry claim` `entry` 6 12 TRUE TRUE `ind replicates A` FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the entry is sufficient` (`ind entry claim` `entry` 6 12 TRUE TRUE `ind replicates A` FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `ind entry credit in` (`the Agencies' reading of the entry claim` (`ind entry claim` `entry` 6 12 TRUE TRUE `ind replicates A` FALSE FALSE)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- [S1] "rapid enough to replace lost competition BEFORE any effect ... may occur": later, or at the same time, is not
-- before.
#ASSERT NOT (`the entry is timely` (`ind entry claim` `entry` 18 12 TRUE TRUE `ind replicates A` FALSE FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`the entry is timely` (`ind entry claim` `entry` 12 12 TRUE TRUE `ind replicates A` FALSE FALSE))
-- [M2] "the entry must be durable" (under Timeliness).
#ASSERT NOT (`the entry is timely` (`ind entry claim` `entry` 6 12 FALSE TRUE `ind replicates A` FALSE FALSE))
#ASSERT `ind entry credit in` (`the Agencies' reading of the entry claim` (`ind entry claim` `entry` 6 12 FALSE TRUE `ind replicates A` FALSE FALSE)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- [M1] not likely.
#ASSERT `ind entry credit in` (`the Agencies' reading of the entry claim` (`ind entry claim` `entry` 6 12 TRUE FALSE `ind replicates A` FALSE FALSE)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- [M3] "replicate the scale, strength, and durability of one of the merging parties".
#ASSERT NOT (`the entry is sufficient` (`ind entry claim` `entry` 6 12 TRUE TRUE (LIST `ind compared` "A" TRUE TRUE FALSE) FALSE FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`the entry is sufficient` (`ind entry claim` `entry` 6 12 TRUE TRUE EMPTY FALSE FALSE))
#ASSERT `the entry is sufficient` (`ind entry claim` `entry` 6 12 TRUE TRUE (LIST `ind compared` "A" TRUE TRUE FALSE, `ind compared` "B" TRUE TRUE TRUE) FALSE FALSE)
-- [M4] "typically do not credit entry that depends on lessening competition in other markets".
#ASSERT `ind entry credit in` (`the Agencies' reading of the entry claim` (`ind entry claim` `entry` 6 12 TRUE TRUE `ind replicates A` TRUE FALSE)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- [M5] footnote 65: repositioning is evaluated like entry, but not if it reduces competition where it comes from.
#ASSERT `ind entry credit in` (`the Agencies' reading of the entry claim` (`ind entry claim` `repositioning` 6 12 TRUE TRUE `ind replicates A` FALSE FALSE)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`the supply response is a cognizable rebuttal` (`ind entry claim` `repositioning` 6 12 TRUE TRUE `ind replicates A` FALSE TRUE))
#ASSERT `ind entry credit in` (`the Agencies' reading of the entry claim` (`ind entry claim` `repositioning` 6 12 TRUE TRUE `ind replicates A` FALSE TRUE)) EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `N. Efficiencies: 3.3 [pdf pages 33 and 34 of 51]; footnotes 70 [pdf page 33] and 71 [pdf page 34]`

-- Parameters, in the order of the claim: vague, in the relevant market, substantial benefits, alternatives, contract
-- impractical evidence, verified, merely benefit the merging firms, prevents within a short period, anticompetitive
-- worsening, separate-market decrease, nature/magnitude/likelihood, may tend to create a monopoly, would prevent it.
GIVEN vague IS A BOOLEAN
      inmarket IS A BOOLEAN
      substantial IS A BOOLEAN
      alternatives IS A LIST OF `Alternative way of achieving the benefits`
      impractical IS A BOOLEAN
      verified IS A BOOLEAN
      merely IS A BOOLEAN
      prevents IS A BOOLEAN
      worsening IS A BOOLEAN
      separate IS A BOOLEAN
      magnitude IS A BOOLEAN
      monopoly IS A BOOLEAN
      preventsmonopoly IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Efficiencies claim`
`ind eff` MEANS `Efficiencies claim` WITH
    `the claim is vague or speculative` IS vague
    `the benefits are in the relevant market where competition may be lessened` IS inmarket
    `the merger would produce substantial competitive benefits` IS substantial
    `alternatives that could achieve the benefits` IS alternatives
    `there is evidence that a contract to achieve the efficiencies would not be practical` IS impractical
    `the benefits have been verified by reliable methodology not dependent on the parties' subjective predictions` IS verified
    `the efficiencies merely benefit the merging firms` IS merely
    `credible evidence shows the benefits will, within a short period, prevent the risk of a substantial lessening of competition in the relevant market` IS prevents
    `the benefits result from an anticompetitive worsening of terms for trading partners` IS worsening
    `the benefits reflect or require a decrease in competition in a separate market` IS separate
    `the efficiencies are of a nature, magnitude and likelihood that no substantial lessening of competition is threatened in any relevant market` IS magnitude
    `the merger may tend to create a monopoly` IS monopoly
    `the efficiencies would prevent the creation of a monopoly` IS preventsmonopoly

GIVEN f IS AN `Efficiencies finding`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`ind cognizable` MEANS f's `the efficiencies are cognizable`

GIVEN f IS AN `Efficiencies finding`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`ind eff credit` MEANS f's `the Agencies credit the efficiencies as rebutting the evidence of harm`

-- [N1] all four criteria and the magnitude test: cognizable and credited.
#ASSERT `ind cognizable` (`the Agencies' reading of the efficiencies claim` (`ind eff` FALSE TRUE TRUE EMPTY TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE))
#ASSERT `ind eff credit` (`the Agencies' reading of the efficiencies claim` (`ind eff` FALSE TRUE TRUE EMPTY TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE))
-- [N2] footnote 70: "If inter-firm collaborations are achievable by contract, they are not merger specific."
#ASSERT NOT (`the efficiencies are merger-specific` (`ind eff` FALSE TRUE TRUE (LIST `contracts between the merging firms`) FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE))
-- CORRECTED after the first run (the test author's error, not the encoding's): this input says a contract COULD
-- achieve the benefits and also that a contract would not be practical, which contradict each other. The first
-- version expected TRUE; footnote 70's first sentence answers the input as written: not merger-specific.
#ASSERT NOT (`the efficiencies are merger-specific` (`ind eff` FALSE TRUE TRUE (LIST `contracts between the merging firms`) TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE))
-- Evidence that a contract would not be practical, and no alternative that could achieve the benefits: merger-specific.
#ASSERT `the efficiencies are merger-specific` (`ind eff` FALSE TRUE TRUE EMPTY TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- p33: organic growth that could achieve the benefits.
#ASSERT NOT (`the efficiencies are merger-specific` (`ind eff` FALSE TRUE TRUE (LIST `organic growth of one of the merging firms`) TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE))
-- [S2] footnote 70 "ONLY in the presence of evidence that a contract ... would not be practical": no such evidence.
#ASSERT NOT (`the efficiencies are merger-specific` (`ind eff` FALSE TRUE TRUE EMPTY FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE))
-- p33 "substantial competitive benefits".
#ASSERT NOT (`the efficiencies are merger-specific` (`ind eff` FALSE TRUE FALSE EMPTY TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE))
-- [N3] "verifiable, and have been verified".
#ASSERT NOT (`the efficiencies are verified` (`ind eff` FALSE TRUE TRUE EMPTY TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`ind cognizable` (`the Agencies' reading of the efficiencies claim` (`ind eff` FALSE TRUE TRUE EMPTY TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE)))
-- p34 "To the extent efficiencies merely benefit the merging firms, they are not cognizable."
#ASSERT NOT (`the efficiencies prevent a reduction in competition` (`ind eff` FALSE TRUE TRUE EMPTY TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`the efficiencies prevent a reduction in competition` (`ind eff` FALSE TRUE TRUE EMPTY TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE))
-- [N4] p33 "nor will they credit benefits outside the relevant market".
#ASSERT NOT (`ind eff credit` (`the Agencies' reading of the efficiencies claim` (`ind eff` FALSE FALSE TRUE EMPTY TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE)))
-- p34 "Not Anticompetitive"; [N5] footnote 71.
#ASSERT NOT (`the efficiencies are not anticompetitive` (`ind eff` FALSE TRUE TRUE EMPTY TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`the efficiencies are not anticompetitive` (`ind eff` FALSE TRUE TRUE EMPTY TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE))
-- p34: cognizable but not of the nature, magnitude and likelihood needed.
#ASSERT `ind cognizable` (`the Agencies' reading of the efficiencies claim` (`ind eff` FALSE TRUE TRUE EMPTY TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`ind eff credit` (`the Agencies' reading of the efficiencies claim` (`ind eff` FALSE TRUE TRUE EMPTY TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)))
-- [N6] p34 "Cognizable efficiencies that would not prevent the creation of a monopoly cannot justify a merger that may
-- tend to create a monopoly."
#ASSERT NOT (`ind eff credit` (`the Agencies' reading of the efficiencies claim` (`ind eff` FALSE TRUE TRUE EMPTY TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE)))
#ASSERT `ind eff credit` (`the Agencies' reading of the efficiencies claim` (`ind eff` FALSE TRUE TRUE EMPTY TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE))
-- p33 "will not credit vague or speculative claims".
#ASSERT NOT (`ind eff credit` (`the Agencies' reading of the efficiencies claim` (`ind eff` TRUE TRUE TRUE EMPTY TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE)))

-- [S3] footnote 31(b) [pdf page 17]: contracts short of a merger could eliminate double marginalization.
GIVEN b IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Double marginalization claim`
`ind dm` MEANS `Double marginalization claim` WITH
    `(a) the merged firm will be more vertically integrated as a result of the merger` IS TRUE
    `(b) contracts short of a merger have eliminated or could eliminate double marginalization` IS b
    `(c) the merged firm has the incentive to reduce price, given the effect on its sales of the related product to rivals` IS TRUE

GIVEN f IS A `Double marginalization finding`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`ind dm not specific` MEANS f's `the double marginalization claim is not merger-specific`

#ASSERT `ind dm not specific` (`the Agencies' reading of the double marginalization claim` (`ind dm` TRUE))
#ASSERT NOT (`ind dm not specific` (`the Agencies' reading of the double marginalization claim` (`ind dm` FALSE)))

§§ `O. SSNIP, HMT and critical loss: 4.3.A and 4.3.B [pdf pages 42 to 44 of 51]; footnote 84 [pdf page 44]; 4.3.C [pdf pages 44 and 45]`

-- [O1] "a SSNIP of five percent of the price"; "may consider ... a price increase that is larger or smaller".
#ASSERT `the SSNIP percentage of` `five percent, as the Agencies often use` EQUALS 5
#ASSERT `the SSNIP percentage of` (`another percentage the Agencies consider` 10) EQUALS 10
#ASSERT `the SSNIP on a price of` `five percent, as the Agencies often use` 200 EQUALS JUST 10
#ASSERT `the SSNIP on a price of` (`another percentage the Agencies consider` 10) 200 EQUALS JUST 20
-- [S11] p44 pipeline: implicit price = price sold for minus price paid.
#ASSERT `the implicit price of the pipeline's service` 50 58 EQUALS 8
GIVEN name IS A STRING
      ssnipt IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Product in the candidate market`
`ind product` MEANS `Product in the candidate market` WITH
    `the product's name` IS name
    `a hypothetical monopolist likely would undertake at least a SSNIPT on it` IS ssnipt

-- [O2] footnote 84 and the HMT answer: a relevant market is not a finding of harm. HMT p42: "at least one product".
#ASSERT `the HMT answer for` (LIST `ind product` "x" TRUE, `ind product` "y" FALSE) EQUALS JUST `the candidate market is a relevant antitrust market, by the HMT; this is not a finding of harm`
#ASSERT `the HMT answer for` (LIST `ind product` "y" FALSE) EQUALS JUST `the HMT does not show the candidate market to be a relevant antitrust market`
-- p41-42: "any one or more of the following" tools.
#ASSERT `a relevant antitrust market is identified, by the tools of 4.3` (LIST `practical indicia`)
#ASSERT NOT (`a relevant antitrust market is identified, by the tools of 4.3` EMPTY)
-- [O3] p44 "raises the hypothetical monopolist's profits if the predicted loss is less than the critical loss".
#ASSERT `the worsening raises the hypothetical monopolist's profits, by critical loss` 10 20
#ASSERT NOT (`the worsening raises the hypothetical monopolist's profits, by critical loss` 20 20)
#ASSERT NOT (`the worsening raises the hypothetical monopolist's profits, by critical loss` 30 20)
-- p44 recapture: "profitable when ... the incremental profits from the increased price plus the incremental profits
-- from the recaptured sales ... exceed the profits lost".
GIVEN price IS A NUMBER
      recaptured IS A NUMBER
      lost IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Recapture facts`
`ind recapture` MEANS `Recapture facts` WITH
    `incremental profits from the increased price` IS price
    `incremental profits from the sales recaptured by other products in the candidate market` IS recaptured
    `profits lost on sales diverted outside the candidate market` IS lost

#ASSERT `the price increase is profitable, by recapture` (`ind recapture` 50 30 70)
#ASSERT NOT (`the price increase is profitable, by recapture` (`ind recapture` 50 20 70))
#ASSERT NOT (`the price increase is profitable, by recapture` (`ind recapture` 40 20 70))

-- [S13] critical loss in units: the number of lost unit sales that leaves profits unchanged.
GIVEN cost IS A NUMBER
      increase IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Breakeven facts`
`ind breakeven at` MEANS `Breakeven facts` WITH
    `unit sales before the worsening of terms` IS 1000
    `the price before` IS 100
    `incremental cost per unit` IS cost
    `the price increase, as a fraction of the price` IS increase

GIVEN cost IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Breakeven facts`
`ind breakeven` MEANS `ind breakeven at` cost 0.05

#ASSERT `ind within` (`the critical loss, in units, of` (`ind breakeven` 60)) 111.11 111.12
-- p45 "Higher pre-merger margins thus indicate ... a smaller critical loss": cost 20 (margin 80%) gives about 58.82.
#ASSERT `ind within` (`the critical loss, in units, of` (`ind breakeven` 20)) 58.82 58.83

§§ `P. Diversion and upward pricing pressure: 4.2.B [pdf page 38 of 51]; footnote 72 [pdf page 37]`

GIVEN lost IS A NUMBER
      diverted IS A NUMBER
      revenues IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Diversion facts`
`ind diversion` MEANS `Diversion facts` WITH
    `unit sales lost by the first product` IS lost
    `units diverted to the second product` IS diverted
    `the second product's price` IS 50
    `incremental cost of the diverted sales, per unit` IS 20
    `revenues lost by the first firm` IS revenues

-- [P1] "the fraction of unit sales lost by the first product ... that would be diverted to the second product".
#ASSERT `the diversion ratio of` (`ind diversion` 100 30 3000) EQUALS JUST 0.3
-- [P2] units diverted x (second price - incremental cost) = 30 x 30.
#ASSERT `the value of diverted sales of` (`ind diversion` 100 30 3000) EQUALS 900
-- [P3] value of diverted sales / revenues lost by the first firm.
#ASSERT `the upward pricing pressure indicator of` (`ind diversion` 100 30 3000) EQUALS JUST 0.3
-- p38 aggregate diversion ratio to a group.
#ASSERT `the aggregate diversion ratio of` 100 (LIST 20, 30) EQUALS JUST 0.5
-- [P4] footnote 72: margin = incremental revenue - incremental cost.
#ASSERT `the margin on incremental units of` 100 60 EQUALS 40

§§ `Q. Market participants, shares and geography: 4.3.D.1 [pdf page 45 of 51]; 4.3.D.2 [pdf pages 46 and 47]; 4.4.A [pdf pages 50 and 51]; 4.4.B [pdf page 51]`

-- [S5] targeting needs different terms AND no likely defeat by arbitrage.
#ASSERT `targeting is feasible, so a market around the targeted customers may be identified` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`targeting is feasible, so a market around the targeted customers may be identified` TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`targeting is feasible, so a market around the targeted customers may be identified` FALSE FALSE)

-- [S4] A sells 60 from a store in the region to customers who travelled in; B sells 40 from the region to the region;
-- C sells 60 from outside the region to customers in it.
GIVEN seller IS A STRING
      amount IS A NUMBER
      fromin IS A BOOLEAN
      toin IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Sale`
`ind sale` MEANS `Sale` WITH
    `the seller` IS seller
    `the amount of the sale` IS amount
    `made from a supplier location in the region` IS fromin
    `made to a customer location in the region` IS toin

GIVETH A LIST OF `Sale`
`ind sales` MEANS LIST `ind sale` "A" 60 TRUE FALSE, `ind sale` "B" 40 TRUE TRUE, `ind sale` "C" 60 FALSE TRUE

#ASSERT `the sale is counted in the geographic market` `based on the locations of suppliers` (`ind sale` "A" 60 TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the sale is counted in the geographic market` `based on the locations of customers` (`ind sale` "A" 60 TRUE FALSE))
#ASSERT `the sale is counted in the geographic market` `based on the locations of customers` (`ind sale` "C" 60 FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the sale is counted in the geographic market` `based on the locations of suppliers` (`ind sale` "C" 60 FALSE TRUE))
#ASSERT `the seller's share of the geographic market, in percent` `based on the locations of suppliers` `ind sales` "A" EQUALS JUST 60
#ASSERT `the seller's share of the geographic market, in percent` `based on the locations of customers` `ind sales` "C" EQUALS JUST 60
#ASSERT `the seller's share of the geographic market, in percent` `based on the locations of customers` `ind sales` "A" EQUALS JUST 0

-- 4.4.A: who is a participant. Parameters: currently supplies, vertically integrated, committed, rapid, sunk costs,
-- idle or swing capacity.
GIVEN supplies IS A BOOLEAN
      vertical IS A BOOLEAN
      committed IS A BOOLEAN
      rapid IS A BOOLEAN
      sunk IS A BOOLEAN
      idle IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Firm considered as a participant`
`ind participant` MEANS `Firm considered as a participant` WITH
    `the firm currently supplies products in the relevant market` IS supplies
    `the firm is vertically integrated, and including it accurately reflects its competitive significance` IS vertical
    `the firm has committed to entering the market in the near future` IS committed
    `the firm very likely would rapidly enter with direct competitive impact on a small but significant change in conditions` IS rapid
    `the firm would incur significant sunk costs to enter` IS sunk
    `the firm has idle or swing capacity` IS idle

-- [Q1]
#ASSERT `the firm's participation in the relevant market` (`ind participant` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `a participant: it currently supplies the relevant market`
#ASSERT `the firm's participation in the relevant market` (`ind participant` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `a participant: it has committed to entering in the near future`
-- [S12]
#ASSERT `the firm's participation in the relevant market` (`ind participant` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `a participant: a vertically integrated firm`
-- [Q2] rapid entrant only "without incurring significant sunk costs".
#ASSERT `the firm's participation in the relevant market` (`ind participant` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `a participant: a rapid entrant`
#ASSERT `the firm's participation in the relevant market` (`ind participant` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS `not a participant: its entry, if any, is considered under Section 3.2`
-- [Q3] "a firm's possession of idle or swing capacity alone does not make that firm a rapid entrant".
#ASSERT `the firm's participation in the relevant market` (`ind participant` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS `not a participant: its entry, if any, is considered under Section 3.2`

-- 4.4.B then Guideline 1: revenues 300 and 200 for the parties, 500 for a rival give shares 30, 20, 50; change 1,200;
-- post HHI 5,000: presumption.
GIVEN name IS A STRING
      amount IS A NUMBER
      party IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Firm's measured amount`
`ind measured` MEANS `Firm's measured amount` WITH
    `the measured firm` IS name
    `its amount on the measure` IS amount
    `the measured firm is a party to the merger` IS party

GIVETH A LIST OF `Firm's measured amount`
`ind revenues` MEANS LIST `ind measured` "A" 300 TRUE, `ind measured` "B" 200 TRUE, `ind measured` "C" 500 FALSE

GIVEN m IS A MAYBE (LIST OF `Firm in the relevant market`)
GIVETH A MAYBE `Guideline 1 finding`
`ind G1 of maybe` MEANS
    CONSIDER m
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST market THEN `the Agencies' reading under Guideline 1 of` market

#ASSERT `ind change in` (`ind G1 of maybe` (`the market shares on the measure` `ind revenues`)) EQUALS JUST 1200
#ASSERT `ind post HHI in` (`ind G1 of maybe` (`the market shares on the measure` `ind revenues`)) EQUALS JUST 5000
#ASSERT `ind presumption in` (`ind G1 of maybe` (`the market shares on the measure` `ind revenues`)) EQUALS JUST `ind PRESUME`

§§ `R. Inputs the text gives no answer for: each should come back NOTHING`

-- [R1] shares summing to 80.
#ASSERT `ind G1` (LIST `a party with a share of` "A" 50, `a rival with a share of` "B" 30) EQUALS NOTHING
