-- a foreclosure share over 100, and a negative one.
#ASSERT `the Agencies' reading under Guideline 5 of` (`ind G5 facts` (JUST 150) FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the Agencies' reading under Guideline 5 of` (`ind G5 facts` (JUST (0 MINUS 5)) FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- an HHI over 10,000, and a negative HHI, for the market entered.
#ASSERT `the Agencies' reading under Guideline 4 of` (`ind G4 facts` (`a market whose HHI is` 12000) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the Agencies' reading under Guideline 4 of` (`ind G4 facts` (`a market whose HHI is` (0 MINUS 5)) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- [R11-related] a negative liquidation value or a negative offer price.
#ASSERT `the offer is a reasonable alternative offer, by footnote 62` (`ind offer` 10 TRUE TRUE TRUE) (0 MINUS 5) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the Agencies' reading of the failing firm claim` (`ind FF claim` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE (0 MINUS 5) EMPTY) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the Agencies' reading of the failing firm claim` (`ind FF claim` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE 100 (LIST `ind offer` (0 MINUS 10) TRUE TRUE TRUE)) EQUALS NOTHING
-- [R11] an offer exactly at liquidation value: footnote 62 is silent.
#ASSERT `the offer is a reasonable alternative offer, by footnote 62` (`ind offer` 100 TRUE TRUE TRUE) 100 EQUALS NOTHING
-- diversion: no units lost; more diverted than lost; negative units.
#ASSERT `the diversion ratio of` (`ind diversion` 0 0 3000) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the diversion ratio of` (`ind diversion` 100 130 3000) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the diversion ratio of` (`ind diversion` (0 MINUS 100) 30 3000) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the upward pricing pressure indicator of` (`ind diversion` 100 30 0) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the aggregate diversion ratio of` 0 (LIST 20, 30) EQUALS NOTHING
-- a SSNIP on a negative price.
#ASSERT `the SSNIP on a price of` `five percent, as the Agencies often use` (0 MINUS 200) EQUALS NOTHING
-- critical loss with a price below incremental cost, and with a negative price increase.
#ASSERT `the critical loss, in units, of` (`ind breakeven` 120) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the critical loss, in units, of` (`ind breakeven at` 60 (0 MINUS 0.05)) EQUALS NOTHING
-- an entry claim with a negative time.
#ASSERT `the Agencies' reading of the entry claim` (`ind entry claim` `entry` (0 MINUS 6) 12 TRUE TRUE `ind replicates A` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- an empty candidate market.
#ASSERT `the HMT answer for` EMPTY EQUALS NOTHING
-- shares on a measure whose total is zero, and with a negative amount.
#ASSERT `the market shares on the measure` (LIST `ind measured` "A" 0 TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the market shares on the measure` (LIST `ind measured` "A" (0 MINUS 50) TRUE, `ind measured` "B" 150 TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- a geographic share when no sale is counted at all.
#ASSERT `the seller's share of the geographic market, in percent` `based on the locations of suppliers` EMPTY "A" EQUALS NOTHING
